    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28704" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῠσαπ-άλλακτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hard to get rid
			of</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοῦσος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Nat.Mul.</u>
					40
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδύναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					959
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσταγμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					10.28
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρρώστημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>PA</u>
					671b9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.</u>
				10a4
			</span></i>: c. gen., -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότεραι τῶν ἐμβρύων</span>
			<i>having difficulty in bringing forth</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>HA</u>
				587b1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀπὸ λόγου</span> a person
				<i>hard to draw away</i> from . . , <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				195c
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἔχειν τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eust.
					1389.46
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eustr.
				<u>in EN</u>
				140.18
			</span></i>.</div>
